um holds a chlorite lingam on a circular yoni pitha. Built of sandstone, the present structure is a recent rebuilding over the remains of an earlier temple and is covered in cement plaster and paint.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":2.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Nilkantheswar Shiva Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"d472ac01-e407-473c-8ecb-eb0850e9d12e","name":"Karna Temple, Karnaprayag","deity":"Surya (via Karna's penance)","sampradaya":"Saura","significance":["Panch Prayag"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Chamoli","town":"Karnaprayag","latitude":30.259,"longitude":79.218,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Alaknanda–Pindar confluence","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Mar–Jun and Sep–Nov.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:22:57.994564+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"The third of the Panch Prayag, at the confluence of the Alaknanda and Pindar rivers — among the widest of the five. The temple, perched on a large boulder at the sangam, marks the spot where Karna of the Mahabharata is said to have performed severe penance to Surya, the sun god, who granted him his celebrated armor and earrings. Local tradition also holds that Krishna performed Karna's last rites at this confluence after the Kurukshetra war.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"कर्ण मंदिर, कर्णप्रयाग","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":99.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":null,"nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Mahabharata tradition; local/regional lore","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"d49ff662-e4ce-4ebe-8e9a-becf0bec8e34","name":"Banni Mata Temple","deity":"Kali","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Himachal Pradesh","district":"Chamba","town":"Badgaram","latitude":32.541,"longitude":76.461,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Tundah Nala River","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient Kali temple in Chamba district at about 2,600 m, at the foot of the Pir Panjal range and surrounded by deep forest. It is also counted as a Shakti temple and lies opposite the Manimahesh peak near Tundah village. The name comes from the many ban, or oak, trees at the site.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kangra Airport, Gaggal","nearest_airport_distance_km":45.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nagrota railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":48.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Banni Mat