 Nandi inside the Bugle Rock park in Basavanagudi, said to be among the largest Nandi temples anywhere. The monolithic stone Nandi is kept continually covered with fresh layers of butter (benne). A Ganesha shrine stands close by. On the last Monday and Tuesday of the month of Karthika a groundnut fair, Kadalekaayi Parishe, is held in the premises and groundnuts are offered to the deity.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kempegowda International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":32,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Krantivira Sangolli Rayanna (Bengaluru) railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Dodda Basavana Gudi)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"d75055d5-6d84-4cf4-9656-c50dc9840bcb","name":"Aranmula Parthasarathy Temple","deity":"Parthasarathy (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Malai Nadu Divya Desam"],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Pathanamthitta","town":"Aranmula","latitude":9.3281,"longitude":76.6879,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Pamba","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; the Aranmula Boat Race (Uthrittathi Vallamkali) falls in Aug/Sep (Malayalam month Chingam) and draws huge crowds.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-06T08:12:33.253723+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the Malai Nadu Divya Desams and one of five Pandava-built shrines of the Chengannur area, tradition crediting this one to Arjuna, with Krishna worshipped here as Parthasarathy, his charioteer form. Tradition holds the deity arrived by raft on six bamboo poles (aru mula), giving the village its name. The famous Aranmula snake-boat race traces to a legend of boats rushing to protect a devotee's offering-laden vessel bound for the temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ആറന്മുള പാര്‍ത്ഥസാരഥി ക്ഷേത്രം","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":97.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chengannur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Mahabharata tradition; local/regional legend","architecture_style":"Kerala style, with 18th-century wall paintings","construction_century":null},{"id":"d75ccd77-3ecf-49be-9773-aef6c8278d61","name":"Pundareekapuram Temple","deity":"Vishnu on Garuda with Bhoodevi","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Kottayam","town":"Thalayolaparambu","latitude":9.79964,"longitude":76.45539,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"vadayattu River","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:59.708182+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A small temple on a rise called Midayikunnam near Thalayolaparambu, Kottayam, Kerala. A tiled, saddle-roofed square enclosure surrounds the square sanctum, and the main image shows Vishnu seated on Garuda with Bhoodevi. It is noted for murals, including Shiva and Parvati, Durga slaying Mahisha, Krishna's childhood, Rama's coronation and Shiva Thandava.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":39.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Vaikam Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Pundareekapuram Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Kerala","construction_century":null},{"id":"d7778be0-65f2-4e4f-985c-5eeb7b314c74","name":"Maluti temples","deity":"Mowlakshi, with Shiva, Durga, Kali and Vishnu","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Jharkhand","district":"Dumka","town":"Maluti","latitude":24.15,"longitude":87.66667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Chila River","river_distance_km":0.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:11.054915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A group of 72 surviving terracotta temples out of an original 108, in the village of Maluti. They were raised between the 17th and 19th centuries by the Baj Basanta kings, whose family deity was the goddess Mowlakshi. Other shrines honour Shiva, Durga, Kali and Vishnu, and the site is the subject of a proposed conservation effort.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kazi Nazrul Islam Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":72.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Pinargaria railwa