eshwar area and over a hundred years old. It has a three-spire structure and holds images of Laxminarayan Dev with Ghanshyam Maharaj, and Radha Krishna Dev with Hari Krishna Maharaj. It belongs to the Vadtal Laxminarayan Dev Gadi. Demand for flowers from such temples helped start Phool Galli.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":15.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Masjid railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Swaminarayan Mandir, Mumbai), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Shikharbaddh, three spires","construction_century":null},{"id":"da096c23-5c9d-43cf-8d80-96535b35fcdd","name":"Sri Moolastaneswara Swamy Temple, Mulapeta","deity":"Shiva as Moolastaneswara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Sri Potti Sriramulu Nellore","town":"Nellore","latitude":14.4483,"longitude":79.9695,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Penna River","river_distance_km":1.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:10:09.085477+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Located at Mulapeta on the west side of Nellore, this temple is described as the oldest Shaiva shrine of the area, dating from the 11th century. It is dedicated to a form of Shiva. Maha Shivaratri is observed here, and the Karthika Masam festivities are an especially important occasion.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":101.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nellore railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Sri Moolastaneswara Swamy Temple, Mulapeta), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":11},{"id":"da242f83-d8f6-4353-b794-c8adf99a2d71","name":"Shri Kedar Temple","deity":"Shiva as Kedareswara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Assam","district":"Kamrup","town":"Hajo","latitude":26.24178,"longitude":91.54397,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Puthimari River","river_distance_km":1.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:24.13334+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A medieval Shiva temple at the top of Madanachala hill in Hajo, Assam. The central chamber has a linga regarded as swayambhu, and the temple and adjacent walls were built by Ahom king Rajeswara Singha in 1753.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Lokpriya Gopinath Bordoloi International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":15.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Agthori railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":15,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Kedar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":18},{"id":"da3a6568-d3de-4d27-bef4-bf8e08546c40","name":"Belur Math, Howrah","deity":"Sri Ramakrishna Paramahamsa (his relics enshrined in the main temple); also shrines to Sarada Devi and Swami Vivekananda within the complex","sampradaya":null,"significance":["Ramakrishna Math and Mission headquarters"],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Howrah","town":"Belur","latitude":22.6325,"longitude":88.35639,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Hooghly","river_distance_km":0,"best_season_notes":"Kumari Puja and the birthday observances of Sri Ramakrishna, Sarada Devi and Swami Vivekananda are especially significant here, alongside Durga Puja, Kali Puja, Janmashtami and Shivaratri.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T09:14:22.726852+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-22T09:14:22.726852+00:00","sthala_purana":"The land was purchased on 4 March 1897 by Swami Vivekananda; Sri Ramakrishna's relics were installed on 9 December 1898, and the main temple was consecrated on 14 January 1938 — all well-documented institutional history, not legend.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Approximate hours per tourism sources, not an official published schedule: April–Sept roughly 6am–11:30am and 4–7pm; Oct–March roughly 6:30am–11:30am and 3:30–6pm; sandhya arati around 5:30pm.","accessibility_notes":"Reachable by EMU suburban train to Belur Math railway station (adjacent to the complex), by ferry across the Hooghly from the Dakshineswar/Kolkata side, or by road from Howrah.","nearest_airport_name":"Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose International Airport, Kolkata","nearest_airport_distance_km":20,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Belur Math railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Ramakrishna Math and Mission institutional records","architecture_style":"A deliberately syncretic \"Symphony in Architecture\" completed 1935–1938: a South Indian gopuram-style entrance, Buddhist stupa elements, a Renaissance dome modelled on Florence Cathedral, a Christian-cross ground plan, and Rajput elements, meant to symbolise the unity of religions. 34.3m tall, built largely of Chunar stone.","construction_century":20},{"id":"da3f491c-04a3-487d-9f1a-e2fc3e883dee","name":"Pachala Someswara Temple","deity":"Shiva as Someswara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Nalgonda","town":"Panagal","latitude":17.07967,"longitude":79.2882,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shaiva temple at Panagal in Nalgonda district, a popular pilgrimage site at Maha Shivaratri. Its deity is carved from green onyx, which gives the temple its name, as pacha means green in Telugu. It stands near the Chaya Someswara Temple and dates to the 11th or 12th century, probably under the Kunduru Chodas and Kakatiya Prataparudra I.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Rajiv Gandhi International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":