8:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Local tradition holds that a devotee unable to travel to Tirupati was directed in a dream by Lord Venkateswara to Chilkur, where the idol was found beneath a molehill. The temple's later history is associated with Madanna and Akkanna — though sources disagree on whether the structure itself dates to the 14th century or to their own 17th-century Qutb Shahi era, so no construction century is asserted here. It is best known today for a distinctive practice: there is no hundi (donation box) and no paid \"special\" darshan, and devotees perform 11 circumambulations to make a wish, returning for 108 after it is fulfilled — the basis of its popular \"Visa Balaji\" nickname among US visa applicants.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"RGIA Phase II","nearest_airport_distance_km":17.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Telapur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":13,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local tradition; temple practice as documented by visitors and press coverage","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"db6a5277-4cfa-472f-9cf9-481d82c04905","name":"Durga Mandir, Varanasi","deity":"Durga","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Varanasi","town":"Varanasi","latitude":25.28862,"longitude":82.99928,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Assi River","river_distance_km":0.4,"best_season_notes":"Durga Puja and Navratri are the major festivals; the quietest visiting window is cited as roughly 6–9am.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T10:01:49.265512+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built in the 18th century by Rani Bhabani of Natore, a Bengali queen and patron; the exact year isn't documented. Devi-Bhagavata Purana tradition holds it was built after Durga aided the Kashi Naresh (the king of Kashi) in a military conflict — legend, not verified history. It's popularly nicknamed the \"Monkey Temple\" for its resident monkey population, per tourism sources rather than the temple's own material.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Per tourism sources, not an official schedule: roughly 5am–12pm and 4–9pm. Mangal Aarti around 4am, Bhog Aarti around 12pm, Sandhya Aarti around 7pm, Sayan Aarti around 10pm.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Lal Bahadur Shastri Airport, Varanasi","nearest_airport_distance_km":25,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Banaras (Manduadih) railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Devi-Bhagavata Purana tradition; local and tourism sources","architecture_style":"North Indian Nagara style; distinctive red-ochre colouring, several small shikharas joined together with carved stonework","construction_century":18},{"id":"dc6a6806-5064-4145-9b3b-e23fc85db87b","name":"Yellamma Temple, Saundatti","deity":"Yellamma (Renuka)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Belagavi","town":"Yellamagudda","latitude":15.754,"longitude":75.16,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Malaprabha","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A hilltop temple about 5 km from Saundatti in Karnataka, dedicated to the goddess Yellamma or Renuka, revered as a fertility goddess. The hill overlooks the Malaprabha river and has traces of occupation from the 8th to 11th centuries and earlier megalithic tombs. The temple was historically linked to the Devadasi practice, banned in 1982.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Hubballi Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":44.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Dharwad railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":38.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Yellamma Temple, Saundatti), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"dcbd0068-8812-47b4-90cc-9a8c65befb17","name":"Virateshwar temple","deity":"Shiva as Virateshwar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Madhya Pradesh","town":"Shahdol","latitude":23.299,"longitude":81.356,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Son River","river_distance_km":12.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A roughly 70-foot Shiva temple at Sohagpur in Shahdol district, built by the Kalchuri ruler Yuvarajadeva II between 950 and 1050 CE as a gift for the head of the Golkaki Math. It is protected by the ASI, and a five-day Banganga fair is held in its courtyard.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jabalpur Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":133.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Shahdol railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Virateshwar temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Kalchuri","construction_century":10},{"id":"dccdef71-7094-478b-9ea0-0354c58168bb","name":"Elephanta Caves","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Raigad","town":"Sheva","latitude":18.96333,"longitude":72.93139,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Mithi River","river_distance_km":12.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:59:23.880063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A UNESCO World Heritage cave temple complex on Elephanta Island in Mumbai Harbour, mainly dedicated to Shiva. Five Hindu caves hold basalt rock-cut reliefs, notably the three-faced Sadashiva, Nataraja and Yogishvara. The carvings are generally placed in the 5th to 7th centuries, and much of the art has been damaged.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Navi Mumbai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":14.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sewri railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Elephanta Caves), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Rock-cut cave temples","construction_century":6},{"id":"dd80c595-515a-4b97-bc6d-3ff0b3f63156","name":"Sri Kalahasti Temple (Vayu Sthalam)","deity":"Shiva (Kalahastiswara)","sampradaya":null,"significance":["Pancha Bhoota Sthalam"],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Tirupati","town":"Srikalahasti","latitude":13.75,"longitude":79.7,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The Swarnamukhi river runs directly alongside the temple.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Temple Annaprasadam Hall — free meals, serving thousands daily and tens of thousands during festivals","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.2,"nearest_river_name":"Swarnamukhi","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; often combined with a Tirupati visit, about an hour away.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"The lamps in the sanctum flicker without any draught, which is why this is counted as the air element among the Pancha Bhoota Sthalams. The temple is associated with Kannappa, the hunter-devotee who offered his own eyes to the lingam, and with the spider, serpent and elephant whose worship gives the place its name.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"శ్రీ కాళహస్తి ఆలయం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":21.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sri Kalahasti railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Dravidian; the inner sanctum dates to the 5th century, the outer temple and gopurams to the 11th-century Cholas, and the 120-foot Raja Gopuram to Krishnadevaraya of Vijayanagara in 1516","construction_century":11},{"id":"dd888d02-0f45-40dd-bd60-7d42b143a12a","name":"Vishnu Temple, Vishnuprayag","deity":"Vishnu","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Panch Prayag"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Chamoli","town":"Vishnuprayag","latitude":30.5625,"longitude":79.57528,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Alaknanda–Dhauliganga confluence","river_distance_km":0.05,"best_season_notes":"May–Jun and Sep–Oct; closed off by snow in deep winter and prone to landslides in the monsoon.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:22:57.994564+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"The first of the Panch Prayag going downstream, where the Alaknanda meets the Dhauliganga near Joshimath. Tradition holds that the sage Narada performed penance here to Vishnu, giving the confluence its name. The present Vishnu temple beside the sangam was built in the 19th century by Ahilyabai Holkar, the Maharani of Indore, who endowed temples across many of India's pilgrimage sites.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"विष्णु मंदिर, विष्णुप्रयाग","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":139.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":null,"nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"North Indian hill-temple style, built by Ahilyabai Holkar of Indore","construction_century":19},{"id":"ddbb76f4-4eb4-4093-bd1c-51a71f5ef8bc","name":"Sri Ranganayaka Swamy Temple","deity":"Vishnu as Ranganayaka Swamy","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Wanaparthy","town":"Sri Rangapur","latitude":16.198,"longitude":78.049,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Okacheti Vagu River","river_distance_km":12.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"This temple at Shri Rangapur in Wanaparthy district was built in the 18th century by Raja Baheri Gopal Rao of Wanaparthy, who admired the Srirangam temple and wanted a similar one in his region. It is built in Vijayanagara-style architecture.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Uyyalawada Narasimha Reddy Airport ,   Kurnool","nearest_airport_distance_km":55.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sriramnagar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":22.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Sri Ranganayaka Swamy Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Vijayanagara","construction_century":18},{"id":"ddc42c41-e39f-4967-ac49-d388e9fd906c","name":"Kanipura Sri Gopalakrishna Temple","deity":"Krishna as Bala Gopalakrishna","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Kasaragod","town":"Arikady","latitude":12.59491,"longitude":74.9424,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Shiriya (Sire hole) River","river_distance_km":1.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient Krishna temple at Kumbla north of Kasaragod, counted among the Abhimana Kshethrams of the Vaishnava tradition. According to local belief, the child-form idol was given by Krishna to a sage. Records say King Jayasimha of the Kadamba dynasty renovated it in the 10th century, and the Kumbla Rajas were crowned here.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mangalore International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":40.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kumbala railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Kanipura Sri Gopalakrishna Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":10},{"id":"ddf4c95e-6161-40d8-adc4-928cb3467e3f","name":"Manikarneswar Devalaya","deity":"Shiva as Manikarneswar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Assam","district":"Kamrup Metropolitan","town":"Rajbhawan","latitude":26.20714,"longitude":91.748,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Brahmaputra River","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:47.875457+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple on top of Manikhalaya hill in North Guwahati, Assam. The Ahom king Rajeswar Singha built the present brick temple in 1755 on the star-shaped plan of an earlier stone temple of the tenth or eleventh century. The 1897 earthquake destroyed its shikhara, and it is now roofed with tin.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Lokpriya Gopinath Bordoloi International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":19.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Guwahati railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Manikarneswar Devalaya), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Star-shaped plan, brick","construction_century":18},{"id":"ddfe680a-a609-45ff-bfdf-8165f439288e","name":"Shri Keshavraiji Temple, Bet Dwarka","deity":"Krishna as Keshavraiji","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Gujarat","district":"Devbhumi Dwaraka","town":"Beyt","latitude":22.45194,"longitude":69.09583,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:24.13334+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient Krishna temple on Bet Dwarka island, said to have been built by the Pushkarna Brahmin community. It lies close to Shankh Sarovar, about a kilometre from the jetty and the Dwarkadhish Temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jamnagar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":93.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Okha railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Keshavraiji Temple, Bet Dwarka), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"de14a8a6-660b-4178-9e24-6d6380d85d63","name":"Vadakkunnathan Temple, Thrissur","deity":"Vadakkunnathan (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Thrissur","town":"Thrissur","latitude":10.5276,"longitude":76.2144,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Puzhakkal River","river_distance_km":1.9,"best_season_notes":"Apr–May for Thrissur Pooram, the region's largest temple festival; Oct–Feb otherwise.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the oldest Shiva temples in Kerala, built in the classical Kerala mural-and-gajaprishta style. It hosts the Thrissur Pooram festival on its grounds, famous for its massed caparisoned elephants and percussion ensembles, though the temple itself does not take part in the procession.","etiquette_notes":"Traditional dress code applies: men in mundu/dhoti, women in saree or churidar with a covering dupatta. The temple hosts one of Kerala's largest festivals (Thrissur Pooram) in its outer grounds, though the sanctum itself keeps to normal Kerala temple custom.","native_name":"വടക്കുന്നാഥ ക്ഷേത്രം","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":46.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Punkunnam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Kerala","construction_century":null},{"id":"de6a8714-d935-4499-9947-814f7f952ad5","name":"Paradaresvara Siva Temple","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Khordha","town":"Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation","latitude":20.25306,"longitude":85.84333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dayaa River","river_distance_km":4.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A 13th-century Shiva temple in the old town of Bhubaneswar, dated from its architecture to the Ganga period. It faces east and lies within the Gosagaresvar precinct. The sanctum holds a circular yonipitha, the lingam being missing, and worship continues here.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":3.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Paradaresvara Siva Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":13},{"id"