on","latitude":21.09278,"longitude":81.00611,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Shivnath River","river_distance_km":3.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:27.898205+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple in Rajnandgaon, Chhattisgarh, about 40 km from Durg on the road toward Nagpur. A large Shiva Linga rises at the top of the temple, and a large statue of Nandi stands in front of it.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Swami Vivekananda Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":77.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Rajnandgaon railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Barfani Dham), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"e0f39c38-9c89-45f4-b218-be0d960f7658","name":"Cheluvanarayana Swamy Temple, Melkote","deity":"Cheluvanarayana (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Mandya","town":"Melkote","latitude":12.6614,"longitude":76.6497,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The Kalyani temple tank sits within the complex.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kalyani (temple tank)","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb. Vairamudi Brahmotsavam (Mar/Apr) is the largest festival.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T13:44:40.752775+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A hill kshetra closely associated with Ramanujacharya, who is said to have lived here for over a decade and reorganised its worship. It remains a major centre of the Sri Vaishnava tradition and of Sanskrit learning.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ಚೆಲುವನಾರಾಯಣ ಸ್ವಾಮಿ ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನ","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mysore Mandakalli Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":47.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Byadarahalli railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":20.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Vesara (Hoysala)","construction_century":13},{"id":"e126f12b-30a5-416f-9a61-7ca49182c938","name":"Raghunath Temple, Devprayag","deity":"Raghunath (Rama)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Panch Prayag"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Tehri Garhwal","town":"Devprayag","latitude":30.14556,"longitude":78.56444,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Bhagirathi–Alaknanda confluence (source of the Ganga)","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Mar–Jun and Sep–Nov.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:22:57.994564+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"The last and most revered of the Panch Prayag: here the Bhagirathi meets the Alaknanda, and their combined waters take on the name Ganga for the rest of their course to the sea. The temple, traditionally consecrated by Adi Shankaracharya in the 8th century and later expanded under the Garhwal kingdom, is among the oldest continuously worshipped shrines in the Himalaya. Rama is held to have performed penance here to atone for killing Ravana, and the deity is worshipped as Raghunathji.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"रघुनाथ मंदिर, देवप्रयाग","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":37.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Rishikesh railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":27,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"North Indian Himalayan hill-temple style; expanded under the Garhwal kingdom","construction_century":8},{"id":"e12c72fb-1f23-46d1-b5ec-afb3ac1c97b5","name":"Lodheshwar Mahadev Mandir","deity":"Shiva as Lodheshwar Mahadev","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Bahraich","town":"Kaiserganj","latitude":27.09556,"longitude":81.48472,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ghaghara River","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple at Mahadeva village, Ram Nagar tehsil, Barabanki district, Uttar Pradesh. Its Shivling is said to be among the rare 52 found on Shakti Pithas, and Lodhi Rajputs treat Lodheshwar as their family deity. The article says the temple is mentioned several times in the Mahabharata.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evenin