a temple in Thiruvaloor, Alangad, Ernakulam district, Kerala. The idol is believed to be an Agni Pratishta, with Shiva's third eye open, and a pond east of the sanctum is said to be placed to offset the idol's heat. Ganapati is the other deity, and the neighbouring Keezhanikavu shrine houses Vishnu, Bhagavati and Nagas.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":11,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Aluva railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Thiruvaloor Mahadeva Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"e53a5d54-d36a-40d4-88d8-a50826551588","name":"Vindhyavasini Temple","deity":"Vindhyavasini (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Mirzapur","town":"Vindhyachal","latitude":25.29,"longitude":82.497,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The Ganga flows right past the temple town.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Temple langar/free food arrangements, primarily for the poor and visiting sadhus","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.3,"nearest_river_name":"Ganga","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Nov and Feb–Mar avoid the worst of the Gangetic plain's winter fog; Navratri draws very large crowds in this stretch regardless.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"The sthala purana relates that Shiva drank the halahala poison churned from the ocean and held it in his throat, which turned blue. His consort here is Vishalakshi, and the Ganga passes at the foot of the temple town.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"विंध्यवासिनी मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Lal Bahadur Shastri International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":40.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ahimanpur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Devi Bhagavata Purana / Shakti Peetha tradition (Sati-limb legend)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"e566507a-48ee-4bca-b1eb-37065bcc63cb","name":"Punkunnam Seetha Ramaswamy Temple","deity":"Rama and Sita","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Thrissur","town":"Punkunnam","latitude":10.53852,"longitude":76.20152,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Puzhakkal River","river_distance_km":1.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:53.924452+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Rama temple in the Pushpagiri agraharam of Thrissur city where Rama and Sita stand on the same pedestal in the sanctum. It also has shrines for Lakshmana and Hanuman, plus separate Ayyappan and Shiva temples. A justice of the Cochin Court built it, with consecration held in 1895.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":48,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Punkunnam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Punkunnam Seetha Ramaswamy Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Kerala temple","construction_century":19},{"id":"e5e98a15-a736-480b-8403-c46d405bb58f","name":"Garjiya Devi","deity":"Garjiya Devi","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Nainital","town":"Nainital","latitude":29.4941,"longitude":79.14123,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kosi","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:53.924452+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Devi shrine on a large rock above the Kosi river near Ramnagar in Uttarakhand, at the edge of Corbett National Park. Garjiya is believed to be a form of Parvati. Crowds gather at Kartik Poornima, and the temple also holds a 9th-century black granite statue of Lakshmi-Narayan.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Pantnagar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":60.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ramnagar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":11.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Garjiya Devi), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"e601fb7b-d87a-4bc5-aedd-99c0399fb6e4","name":"Vedapureeswarar Temple, Puducherry","deity":"Vedapurishvarar (Shiva) and Tripurasundari (Parvati)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Puducherry","district":"Puducherry","town":"Puducherry","latitude":11.9399,"longitude":79.8298,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Chenjiyaru River","river_distance_km":6.8,"best_season_notes":"Brahmotsavam in Vaikasi (May–June), Annabhishekam in Aippasi (Oct–Nov) and Maha Shivaratri in Masi (Feb–Mar) are the major festivals.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-25T13:54:12.118115+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Per Wikipedia the temple dates to 1674, was destroyed in 1748 by French troops during religious riots, and was rebuilt in 1788 by Divan Kandappa Mudaliar through public contributions. Only one source was checked for this account.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Per aggregator sites, not an official schedule: roughly 6am–12:30pm and 4:30–8pm.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Puducherry Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Puducherry Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Vedapureeswarar Temple, Pondicherry)","architecture_style":"Dravidian; seven-tiered rajagopuram of about 23 m, granite enclosure and a temple tank","construction_century":18},{"id":"e632ffcc-9a5a-492f-bd95-71ebab3b6fcf","name":"Jagannath Temple, Puri","deity":"Jagannath (Krishna/Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Char Dham"],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Puri","town":"Puri","latitude":19.8135,"longitude":85.8312,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The temple is a short walk from Puri's beach on the Bay of Bengal.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"brahmin_run_kitchen","food_source_name":"Sri Jagannath Temple Ananda Bazaar (Mahaprasad, cooked by the temple's traditional Suar/Mahasuar cooks)","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.2,"nearest_river_name":"Bay of Bengal","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Feb; plan around Rath Yatra (June/July) only if you want the festival crowds, and note that Odisha's coast carries real cyclone risk in Oct–Nov, ahead of its calmer, cooler winter.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-04T08:49:12.455773+00:00","sthala_purana":"The deities here are carved from neem wood rather than stone, and are replaced in the Nabakalebara rite when a particular conjunction of the calendar occurs. Tradition relates that the sculptor Vishwakarma worked behind closed doors on condition of not being disturbed, and that the forms remained unfinished when the door was opened early — which is why Jagannath, Balabhadra and Subhadra are worshipped in that form.","etiquette_notes":"Only Hindus are permitted inside the temple; a viewing platform outside is available for others. No leather items (belts, wallets, bags) are allowed past the security check, and phones/cameras are generally restricted near the sanctum.","native_name":"ଶ୍ରୀ ଜଗନ୍ନାଥ ମନ୍ଦିର","morning_opens_at":"06:00:00","morning_closes_at":"12:00:00","evening_opens_at":"16:00:00","evening_closes_at":"22:00:00","timings_notes":"The temple is on Chakratirtha beach; the Rath Yatra festival (June/July) suspends normal darshan for its own schedule.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport, Bhubaneswar","nearest_airport_distance_km":60,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Puri Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Kalinga","construction_century":12},{"id":"e65ccc68-b06c-457a-8271-7a25caddd22b","name":"Alampur Papanasi Temples","deity":"Shiva as Nataraja","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Jogulamba Gadwal","town":"Kasipur","latitude":15.87147,"longitude":78.123,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Tungabhadra","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:59:23.880063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A group of twenty-three mostly ruined temples, dated to the 9th-11th centuries and moved to the southwest of Alampuram village in Telangana, near where the Tungabhadra meets the Krishna. The largest, Papanasisesvara, is a square Nagara-style shrine to dancing Shiva. The group is linked to the Kalamukha and Pashupata Shaiva sects.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Uyyalawada Narasimha Reddy Airport ,   Kurnool","nearest_airport_distance_km":18,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Alampur Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Alampur Papanasi Temples), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Nagara","construction_century":9},{"id":"e6775136-2604-4190-988c-129970db70ba","name":"Venugopalaswamy Temple, Karvetinagaram","deity":"Krishna as Venugopala","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Chittoor","town":"Mukkaravaripalle","latitude":13.35,"longitude":79.41,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Nagari River","river_distance_km":0.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:10:09.085477+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Vaishnava temple at Karvetinagaram in Chittoor district, devoted to Krishna in the form of Venugopala, regarded by believers as Vishnu's eighth incarnation. It lies about 58 km from Tirupati and 12 km from Puttur.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":34.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Vepagunta railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":16.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Venugopalaswamy Temple, Karvetinagaram), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"e6b1c0a5-430b-4194-8be7-11f2d78eb055","name":"Suryanar Kovil","deity":"Suryanarayana (Surya) / Usha Devi, Pratyusha Devi","sampradaya":"Saura","significance":["Navagraha Sthalam"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Thanjavur","town":"Suryanar Koil","latitude":11.02972,"longitude":79.47778,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cauvery","river_distance_km":3,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; Sundays are considered especially auspicious.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:47:03.785954+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"Unusually among the Navagraha Sthalams, this temple — also called Thirumangalagudi — is dedicated directly to Surya (the Sun) himself rather than housing him as a subsidiary shrine to Shiva, with his consorts Usha Devi and Pratyusha Devi. Tradition holds Shiva blessed the nine planetary deities to make this their principal abode. The present masonry structure dates to the reign of the Chola king Kulottunga I in the 11th century, when it was called Kulottunga Chola-Marttandalaya, with later additions by the Vijayanagara kings.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"சூரியனார் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Thanjavur Air Force Station","nearest_airport_distance_km":52.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Aduturai railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Dravidian (Chola, Vijayanagara)","construction_century":11},{"id":"e6bf7cba-70bb-45f0-b97a-f3c755c9d8c0","name":"Sri Adhipureeshwarar Temple, Pallikaranai","deity":"Adhipureeshwarar (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Pallikaranai","latitude":12.937,"longitude":80.2,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Pallikaranai Marsh","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"An old Shiva temple with its own tank, standing directly on Pallikaranai's main road — distinct from the similarly named Aadhipureeswarar temple of Tiruvottiyur.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":7.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Velachery railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"e6f155fb-05eb-4a1e-b8fe-c195e80370f9","name":"Deo Sun Temple (Deo Surya Mandir)","deity":"Surya, in a west-facing shrine","sampradaya":"Saura","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Aurangabad","town":"Deo","latitude":24.6588,"longitude":84.437,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adari River","river_distance_km":6.7,"best_season_notes":"Chhath, when lakhs of devotees bathe in the temple's kunds and offer arghya to the sun, is the major occasion.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T21:24:56.957301+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Accounts conflict and no single one is asserted. Oral tradition says Vishwakarma built the temple in a single night. The Aurangabad district site attributes it to Bhairavendra, a Chandravanshi king of Umga, in the 15th century, and Wikipedia cites an inscription of 1437 recording his dedication; a 642 CE Gupta-era inscription mentions sun worship in the area but not this temple. Some scholars think it may originally have been a Buddhist temple. The complex has the Brahma, Rudra and Surya kunds.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Gaya International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":52.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Anugrah Narayan Road Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":20,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Deo Surya Mandir); Aurangabad district site","architecture_style":"Described as a mix of Nagara, Dravidian and Vesara elements (Wikipedia); the district site gives a height of about 100 ft","construction_century":null},{"id":"e752c796-a92f-4ea3-9cf9-dafde52d9446","name":"Badhangarhi Temple","deity":"Kali (Dakshineshwar Kali, Bhagwati)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Bageshwar","town":"Garud","latitude":30.0128,"longitude":79.5229,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Gomati River","river_distance_km":3.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An old temple of Kali, worshipped as Dakshineshwar Kali or Bhagwati, in Tharali tehsil of Chamoli Garhwal, Uttarakhand. It is a popular regional deity for people in nearby blocks of Chamoli and Bageshwar. The shrine stands at about 2260 m, 8 km from Gwaldam.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_ai