ity":"Manjunatha (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Dakshina Kannada","town":"Mangaluru","latitude":12.88578,"longitude":74.85558,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Gurupura River","river_distance_km":3.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T09:54:32.209521+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A historic temple in Mangaluru. According to Wikipedia, its in-charge and priests are Shivalli Madhva Brahmins. Little else is recorded in the source, so this entry is deliberately brief.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mangalore International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":8.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mangaluru Central railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Kadri Manjunath Temple)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"e7877cba-8a30-4f66-bfdd-0cb3f23a26c4","name":"Kumararama Bhimeswara Swamy Temple, Samalkota","deity":"Shiva (Bhimeswara)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Pancharama Kshetra"],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Kakinada","town":"Samalkota","latitude":17.0423,"longitude":82.1713,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Pedda Eru River","river_distance_km":12,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; Maha Shivaratri Mahotsavamulu (Feb/Mar) is the principal festival.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T08:35:20.91066+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the five Pancharama Kshetras, believed to hold a fragment of the demon Tarakasura's shattered Atma-linga — this one consecrated, tradition holds, by Kartikeya (Kumara Swamy) himself, giving the site its name Kumararama. The sanctum holds a roughly 14-foot white crystal Shivalinga spanning two floors. The present temple is attributed to the Eastern Chalukya king Chalukya Bhima I (888–918 CE).","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"కుమారారామ భీమేశ్వర స్వామి ఆలయం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Rajahmundry Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":38.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Samalkot Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Dravidian (Eastern Chalukya)","construction_century":9},{"id":"e790a46c-0b37-4ed0-8712-4a1c9dc17636","name":"Hridayaleeswarar Temple, Thirunindravur","deity":"Hridayaleeswarar (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruvallur","town":"Thirunindravur","latitude":13.1073,"longitude":80.0483,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cooum River","river_distance_km":0.8,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built in the 6th century, this Shiva temple is famed as the site of the Nayanmar saint Poosalar's legend: too poor to build a physical temple, he is said to have constructed one entirely in his mind and heart (hridaya) with such devotion that Shiva accepted it as complete — one of the best-loved Bhakti-movement stories in Tamil Shaivism.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":18.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruninravur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey; Periya Puranam","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":6},{"id":"e7a82ad2-a9cb-48b4-b6a0-014525b3e5a7","name":"Jaimangla Garh Temple","deity":"Chandi Mangla Devi","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Begusarai","town":"Jaimangalgarh","latitude":25.5922,"longitude":86.16128,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kanwar Lake","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:01.041713+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient Hindu temple in Begusarai district, Bihar, surrounded by Kanwar Lake. It is dedicated to the goddess Chandi Mangla Devi, whose idol is enshrined within.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Darbhanga Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":71.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sonma Pranpur halt railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Jaimangla Garh Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"e7bfe446-5e82-4d2b-978f-7bbaa8c0f88d","name":"Ranganathaswamy Temple, Srirangam","deity":"Ranganatha (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Pancharanga Kshetram"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruchirappalli","town":"Srirangam","latitude":10.8624,"longitude":78.6905,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The temple sits on an island between two branches of the Kaveri.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Temple annadanam scheme — free meals to several hundred devotees daily, funded by donations","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.2,"nearest_river_name":"Kaveri","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Mar; the largest functioning Hindu temple complex in the world — allow a full day. Srirangam's heaviest rain, like the rest of Tamil Nadu, falls in the northeast monsoon of Oct–Nov rather than the summer months.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-05T16:25:41.548561+00:00","sthala_purana":"Ranganatha reclines here facing south toward Lanka. Tradition relates that Rama gave the image to Vibhishana, who set it down on the Kaveri island while performing his sandhya and found he could not lift it again — so the deity remained, looking toward the kingdom he was to have gone to. Srirangam is reckoned Antya Ranga, the last and southernmost of the five Pancharanga Kshetrams on the Kaveri, following Srirangapatna (Adi Ranga), Shivanasamudra (Madhya Ranga), Koviladi, and Kumbakonam.","etiquette_notes":"Modest dress is expected throughout; some inner areas restrict shorts, sleeveless tops, and leather items. As one of the largest temple complexes in the world, allow time to pass through multiple security and dress checks at different prakarams (enclosures).","native_name":"அரங்கநாதசுவாமி கோயில்","morning_opens_at":"05:00:00","morning_closes_at":"12:30:00","evening_opens_at":"16:00:00","evening_closes_at":"21:30:00","timings_notes":"One of the largest functioning temple complexes in the world — allow extra time to move between its many shrines within these hours.","accessibility_notes":"A large, mostly flat temple-town complex — comfortable for wheelchairs and elderly visitors by South Indian temple standards, though individual shrine thresholds still involve small steps.","nearest_airport_name":"Tiruchirappalli International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":10,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Srirangam Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Naalayira Divya Prabandham (Alvar hymn tradition)","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"e8474579-c909-4ec2-9904-93088d6b6a0a","name":"Pazhamudircholai Murugan Temple","deity":"Murugan (Subrahmanya)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Arupadaiveedu"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Madurai","town":"Pazhamudircholai","latitude":9.9967,"longitude":78.2167,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Uppaar River","river_distance_km":8.2,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T18:27:49.795249+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"The sixth and last of the Arupadaiveedu, set in a forested hill near Madurai, and the only one where Murugan is depicted alongside both his consorts, Valli and Deivanai. Tradition holds this is where the Tamil poet-devotee Avvaiyar, tested by Murugan disguised as a young boy under a tree still worshipped today, was taught a lesson in humility despite her renowned wisdom.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"பழமுதிர்சோலை முருகன் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Madurai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":22.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Madurai East railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":13.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"e8476c1f-373b-4b86-9ddb-c50c1e577417","name":"Ambalappuzha Sree Krishna Swamy Temple","deity":"Vishnu as Krishna (Parthasarathi)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Alappuzha","town":"Ambalapuzha","latitude":9.3836,"longitude":76.3695,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"mammudu thodu River","river_distance_km":1.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:59.708182+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Krishna temple in Ambalappuzha, Alappuzha, Kerala, believed to have been built in the 15th century by a local ruler and counted among the seven great temples of Travancore. The image is likened to Parthasarathi, holding a whip and a conch. It is known for its payasam offering, which tradition says Guruvayoorappan visits daily to accept.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":85.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ambalappuzha railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ambalappuzha Sree Krishna Swamy Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":15},{"id":"e84bad2d-d8fe-4387-a880-54bc0563f222","name":"Kollur Mookambika Temple","deity":"Mookambika (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Udupi","town":"Kollur","latitude":13.8667,"longitude":74.85,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Temple dining hall — free lunch and dinner (rice, sambar, rasam, buttermilk)","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Souparnika","river_distance_km":0.3,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Mar. Navaratri is the principal festival; Kollur sits deep in the Western Ghats monsoon belt, so avoid June–September even more than most Karnataka coastal sites.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"The deity here is held to combine Saraswati, Lakshmi, and Parvati in one form. Tradition credits Adi Shankaracharya with installing the Sri Chakra at the sanctum and fixing the present form of worship during his travels through the region.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ಕೊಲ್ಲೂರು ಮೂಕಾಂಬಿಕಾ ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನ","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":